.SH NAME
git-work-issue-remove - Remove items from list-valued fields of an issue


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work issue remove ID ITEMS|- [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove items from list-valued fields from a JSON object of lists, given as
the argument or on standard input: one RemoveValue operation per item, one commit.

.PP
git work issue remove 2f15 '{"labels":["prio:high"]}'

.PP
Removing an item that is not there changes nothing.
ID is an id prefix or an alias.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print the operations that would be committed, and write nothing

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-issue(1)\fP
